; bfsodium CMAC128 : AES_128 CMAC  NIST SP 800_38B  RFC 4493
;
; NOTE square brackets are brainfuck loops  so comments use braces for counts;
;
; HAND WRITTEN; block/aes128table block/aes128encrypt block/copy16
; block/copy16back block/move16 block/moveup16 and block/shl128 are INCLUDED;
; idiom/xor8 is PASTED ONCE;
;
; IO  in:  key{16}  len{2} LE  message{len}
;     out: tag{16}
;
; THE LENGTH MAY BE ANYTHING  including nought  which is the first mode here
; that can say so; counter mode takes any length because a keystream does not
; care  cipher block chaining takes only whole blocks because it has no
; padding  and this one takes any length because SP 800_38B gives it a
; padding rule and TWO subkeys to tell the padded case from the exact one;
;
; CMAC IS CIPHER BLOCK CHAINING WITH A TWEAK ON THE LAST BLOCK; that is the
; whole of it; X starts at nought rather than at an IV  each block is
; exclusive ored into X and enciphered  and the LAST block takes one further
; exclusive or: with K1 if the message filled it exactly  and with K2 if it
; had to be padded; aes/cmacsubkeys derives and PINS those two against
; RFC 4493's published values  which is why they are not derived blind here;
;
; THE TWEAK IS APPLIED ON EVERY BLOCK  and is NOUGHT on every block but the
; last; Exclusive or with nought is the identity  so the pass costs about
; sixteen runs of idiom/xor8 against the hundred and fourteen million a block
; already costs  and it buys a loop body with no branch in it; That is the
; same argument aes/xtime makes about its own reduction;
;
; THE LAST BLOCK IS KNOWN BY THE COUNT AND NOT BY LOOKING AHEAD; after a
; block has been filled  remaining is nought exactly when that block was the
; last  whether it was filled from the wire or finished with padding; So
; `last` is simply "remaining is nought"  and the only thing padding changes
; is WHICH subkey the tweak comes from;
;
; THE PADDING IS WRITTEN AS IT IS NEEDED  one byte at a time inside the same
; loop that reads: a turn either takes a byte from the wire or writes the
; 0x80 that opens the padding or writes nothing at all  and which of the
; three is decided by two flags rather than by three pieces of code;
;
; THE CONVEYOR CARRIES BOTH OPERANDS; the chain's head is always at @0x3c7
; and the tweak's at @0x3a5  each is lifted out  each slides down  and the
; answer goes in at the chain's tail; Sixteen turns later the chain is back
; in order and THE TWEAK IS EMPTY AGAIN  which is what lets the next block
; start from a clear tweak without clearing it;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x374  the cipher's frame  exactly as block/aes128encrypt maps it
;   @0x375:0x384  savedkey{16}  the key as it came off the wire  never spent
;   @0x385:0x394  K1{16}  the subkey for a message that filled its last block
;   @0x395:0x3a4  K2{16}  the subkey for a message that had to be padded
;   @0x3a5:0x3b4  T{16}   the tweak  NOUGHT except on the last block
;   @0x3c7:0x3d6  X{16}   the chain  and the tag at the end
;   @0x3c7:0x40b  ALSO the block/shl128 frame  during the setup only  which
;                 is why the control cells below start above it
;   @0x40c:0x40d  remaining{2} u16 LE
;   @0x40e        nz      remaining is not nought
;   @0x40f        more    the outer loop runs while this is set
;   @0x410        e       the else arm of the borrowing decrement
;   @0x411:0x412  t u     a copy and its hand back
;   @0x413        padded  set once the 0x80 has been written
;   @0x414        b       the byte this turn folds into the chain
;   @0x415        j       bytes still to fold into this block
;   @0x416        np      the message has NOT been padded yet
;   @0x417        nzn     remaining IS nought
;   @0x418        last    this block is the final one
;   @0x419        lf      the last block was filled exactly  so the tweak is K1
;   @0x41a:0x42a  idiom/xor8 pasted at 1050; result 1050  operands 1051 1052

